Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-08-99||05:36 PM||||Yes it is, but you will not be able to upload pictures (the BBS software can't handle that). I can make a forum section where you can put links to images in your messages that will be automatically embedded. "The Mall" supports images this way, for instance.<p>Or, I could turn on image support in <b>all</b> forums... Let me know what y'all prefer.<p>Ofcourse, any other suggestions for changes/additions to this forum are welcome.<br>
Z||000002||Patrick||04-08-99||06:34 PM||||I vote for turning on image support in ALL forums. Not only would this allow people to show off their Fieros (if they so wished), but it would also allow images to be used when asking or answering technical questions. A picture is worth a thousand words, right? This would help shorten Ogre's <b>long</b> posts.:) (Just kidding, Ogre!)<p>If I understand the process, for anyone to display an image in their post here, this image would have to be at a web site that their post is linked to (using a code). Is that correct? If so, then we'd have to either be making use of an existing image at another web site, or we would have to have uploaded our own image onto our own web page.<p>There is a video related site that I frequent which uses the "commercial" version of this bulletin board. They allow the posting of images there and it has worked out very well. There has NOT been any problem with "inappropriate" images at that site if that is a concern of yours, Cliff.<p>The "commercial" version also has a <b>Search</b> function which comes in real handy when trying to find something which has already been discussed in an earlier thread. I appreciate the fact that this "freeware" version probably doesn't support that feature, but it's something to keep in mind when there are hundreds and hundreds of posts to wade through at this forum in the future.<p>Again, to repeat, I vote <b>"YES"</b> for image support in ALL forums.<p>-Patrick   
Z||000003||PaUL||04-08-99||06:47 PM||||sounds good to me, count me as a YES vote
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||04-09-99||09:24 AM||||Ok, I've switched on the images in <b>all</b> forums!<p>Let me start by showing a picture of my baby, shortly after I had bought it, and before I had it lowered (and before that van crashed into it :( ):<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.pennock.nl/images/myfiero2.jpg"> <p>And a picture of my interior before I installed the digital dashboard:<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.pennock.nl/images/myfiero3.jpg"> <p>Looks like new huh?  :)
Z||000005||PaUL||04-09-99||04:03 PM||||Wow, thats a nice looking Fiero. Ive got to post pics of my custom made dash I made myself. It has the tach in the center like a 911 with the speedo on the left and temp/fuel/volt/oil gauges on the right, all analog. I dont like digital gauges, but I did want to make a digital heads-up type display showing my speed and rpms on the lower winshield. I was going to use 7 segment LEDs for the digits, viewed directly not reflected off the glass for better visibilty in bright light. (I used to be an elec. engineering major a long time ago)
